@startuml activity-signup
' Spec 001 — sign up and confirm (REQ-001-2, REQ-001-3)
title Sign up and confirm email (REQ-001-2, REQ-001-3)

start
:Open sign-up page;
:Enter email, choose role
(Candidate / Employer);
if (Email format valid?) then (no)
  :Show validation error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Role chosen and
not "admin"?) then (no)
  :Show validation error
  (forged "admin" rejected);
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Email already registered?) then (yes)
  :Do nothing
  (no duplicate, no email);
else (no)
  :Create user
  confirmed_at = nil;
  :Create login token
  (expires 15 min);
  :Send magic-link email;
endif
:Go to the log-in page with the same message
either way: "An email was sent to <email>,
please access it to confirm your account.";
:Open email, click link;
if (Token valid, unused,
not expired?) then (no)
  :Show "link invalid or expired";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:The link opens a page: "Welcome <email>";
:Press "Confirm and stay logged in" or
"Confirm and log in only this time";
note right
  Nothing happens until a button is pressed,
  so a mail program that opens links by
  itself cannot use the link up.
end note
:Set confirmed_at = now;
:Revoke ALL tokens for user;
:Create session;
:Logged in;
stop
@enduml
